## Player-visible effect
Options.ini detail (High/Medium/Low/Custom), FPS-limit toggle, tree/shadow/lightmap/cloud/water/heat flags, and static LOD particle/animation presets never apply on the live host. Dynamic LOD during `W3DDisplay::draw` analog uses empty default thresholds, so the 45 Hz execute cap / visual quality do not follow retail options.

## C++
`GameEngine::update` (`GeneralsMD/Code/GameEngine/Source/Common/GameEngine.cpp:732`) always calls `TheRadar->UPDATE()` before audio/client/logic.

`Radar::update` (`Radar.cpp:275-304`) each logic frame:
- expires `m_event[i]` when `active && createFrame && thisFrame > dieFrame`
- if `m_queueTerrainRefreshFrame` is set and `getFrame() - queue > RADAR_QUEUE_TERRAIN_REFRESH_DELAY`, calls `refreshTerrain(TheTerrainLogic)`

Attack/infiltrate/upgrade pings therefore disappear after `dieFrame`, and deferred radar terrain rebuilds (bridges, water, script refresh) actually run.

## Rust
The live host `drive_frame` (`Main/src/cnc_game_engine/run_loop.rs:206-226`) never calls Common `RadarSystem::update`.

`update_internal` ticks `update_runtime_subsystems`, whose Radar slot is `RadarSubsystem::update` (`Main/src/subsystem_manager.rs:690-692`) — a documented no-op ("handled by gamelogic radar notifier"). Main has zero `radar.update(` call sites.

The C++-parity implementation exists (`Common/src/common/system/radar/mod.rs:1080-1119`) and is only invoked from unused crate `GameEngine::update_frame` (`Common/src/common/game_engine.rs:648-650`), not the live run loop.

Distinct from already-filed `addObject` color / `newMap` hook / `tryEvent` distance (hq-jdc6m, hq-xii2r, hq-yfai9).

