Radar event markers (under-attack, infiltration, stealth, upgrade) never time out on the live HUD. Queued terrain refreshes after bridge/water/script changes never rebuild the radar map after the C++ delay.

## C++
`PhysicsBehavior::update` (PhysicsUpdate.cpp:649-663): if OBJECT_STATUS_BRAKING, projectiles get *no* position integration (\"Projectiles never stop braking once they start\" + locomotor 3D cheat owns the pose). Non-projectiles only integrate Z.

## Rust
`update_simple` (`physics_update.rs:764-768`):
```
if obj.test_status(Braking) && !obj.is_kind_of(Projectile) {
    pos.z += state.vel.z;
} else {
    pos += state.vel;
}
```
Braking projectiles take the else branch and full-move.

## Evidence
C++: `if (BRAKING) { if (!PROJECTILE) Adjust_Z; }` — projectile body empty.
Rust condition is `braking && !projectile` for Z-only; projectile+braking → `pos += vel`.

## Player-visible effect
Missiles/shells that entered the braking cheat keep sliding on physics velocity instead of the locomotor snap-to-target, overshooting or weaving off the aim point.

## Split hint
Match the C++ nested if; do not invert the projectile test.

